'''''Digitalis sceptrum''''' (common names; '''sceptre foxglove, bush foxglove''' or '''Madeiran foxglove''')<ref>{{Cite web |title=Digitalis sceptrum {{!}} Isoplexis sceptrum {{!}} Bush Foxglove {{!}} Madeiran Foxglove {{!}} plant lust |url=https://plantlust.com/plants/12684/digitalis-sceptrum/ |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=plantlust.com |language=en}}</ref> is a [[species]] of ''[[Digitalis]]'' from Madeira.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tropicos.org/Name/100365665|title= Digitalis sceptrum in Tropicos}}</ref>

== Description ==
''Digitalis sceptrum'' (previously known as ''isoplexis sceptrum'') is a tender evergreen shrub in the [[Paulownia tomentosa|foxglove]] family, growing up to 1.8m. high. Leaves are toothed and oblong or ovate in shape; flowers consist of [[racemes]] of yellow, orange or tawny russet, often netted with chocolate-brown, appearing in summer.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Digitalis sceptrum {{!}} sceptre foxglove Conservatory Greenhouse/RHS Gardening |url=http://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/234813/digitalis-sceptrum/details |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=www.rhs.org.uk |language=en-gb}}</ref> ''Digitalis sceptrum'' prefers wooded habitats, cloud forests and steep slopes, often near water. It may take up to five years to reach full flowering maturity.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2013-07-15 |title=Plant Portraits: Digitalis sceptrum |url=https://frustratedgardener.com/2013/07/15/plant-portraits-digitalis-sceptrum/ |access-date=2024-06-18 |website=The Frustrated Gardener |language=en-US}}</ref>

